e-control-testing walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the method-selection matrix authored and self-reviewed in-session.

Scope: fictional Alderpoint Mutual (continued): 5 control claims tested.
Artifacts authored:
  - 5-row matrix: control claim as sentence -> primary method -> supporting
    method -> what a pass proves AND what it can't prove:
    1. Portal blocks OWASP Top 10: annual pentest + monthly scans + per-release
       code review (pass proves that-way-that-week, not absence).
    2. Servers match baseline: quarterly config review vs CIS Benchmarks +
       continuous misconfiguration checks (pass proves conformance on sample
       date, not baseline sufficiency).
    3. Firewall rules implement boundary table: quarterly ruleset review +
       annual pentest crossing attempts (configured intent vs running reality).
    4. Phishing reported not clicked: annual scoped social-engineering exercise
       + mailbox log review + training completion (snapshot, not culture).
    5. PII access logged + reviewed: monthly sampled log review + annual
       synthetic transaction proving the detection path end-to-end.
  - Sequencing: cheap before expensive; scan/ruleset outputs handed to pentesters
    as starting intelligence; retest of highs via internal synthetic suite
    within 30 days of claimed remediation.

Self-review checklist (2026-10-10):
  [x] every control has primary + supporting method observing differently
      (configuration vs behavior)
  [x] negative-result discipline: each row states what a pass does NOT prove
  [x] scan treated as weakest assurance, not strongest (the §6 anti-pattern)
  [x] social engineering carries the legal/authorization wrapper
  [x] synthetic transactions test denials, not just the happy path
  [x] methods mapped to verified SP 800-115 catalog (§3 review, §4
      identification/analysis, §5 validation) — PDF fetched in-session
  [x] differentiated from b-methodology (program-level selection, not engagement
      walkthrough)
  [x] no invented statistics; company labeled fictional throughout
Nothing unrun: worked-case lessons have no CLI steps to mark.
